Grove PATCH-22: the ADS test helpers must check the SCRIPTLESS coin's balance

Defect D-7. The shared ADS helpers in tests/basicswap/extended/test_dcr.py --
which every Grove regtest matrix calls, ZEPH's and ZANO's included -- verified
settlement only through the SCRIPTED coin's `gettransaction`. For the
scriptless coin they ran `pass`, twice. For every reverse bid they returned
before reaching any verification at all:

    if reverse_bid:
        return  # TODO

That is half the matrix asserting nothing about where the coins ended up, and
the other half asserting it only for the leg that has a script to fall back
on. A partial settlement, or coins stranded in the wrong wallet, read as a
FULLY GREEN matrix run.

This matters more than the blocked matrices themselves. Every one of ZEPH's
and ZANO's acceptance rows is gated on a green matrix; unblocking the daemons
without fixing this would have produced green results that meant considerably
less than they appeared to -- on precisely the leg (scriptless, no script to
reclaim from) where being wrong is least recoverable.

The fix takes a per-node balance snapshot of every scriptless leg before the
swap, and asserts after settlement that the coins are no longer where they
started. It is deliberately weak in form and strong in placement: it does not
predict WHICH node receives (that differs between forward and reverse bids,
and between the success and refund paths), only that the scriptless leg moved
at all. A stranded or partially-settled leg fails it; a completed one cannot.

Three further properties, each there because its absence is how D-7 survived:

  * a missing baseline is a FAILURE, not a skip -- otherwise the check
    silently degrades back into the `pass` it replaces;
  * the reverse-bid path now runs the balance check BEFORE returning, and the
    return is narrowed to the scripted-side checks that genuinely are
    leader-side only;
  * the two former `pass` branches now assert the baseline was taken, so a
    future edit that removes the snapshot fails loudly at the exact sites that
    used to be silent.

"An xmr-family coin has no gettransaction" was upstream's reason for the
`pass`. It is a good reason not to check it THAT way, and not a reason not to
check it.

Applies on top of PATCH-21.

